D03/01/2024
NStkSplit
YVTSAX
Q20
^
"""
When qif file imported
Then postings created are : PostingRow
| Ref | Date | Account | Amount |
Then holdings are : Holdings
| Account                | Symbol | Shares | Price   | PriceAsOf  |
| Assets:Brokerage:VTSAX | VTSAX  | 200    | 50.0000 | 2024-03-01 |

BusinessRule How a stock split ratio is read
Description The Q field is the new shares per old share, times ten.
Details This is the convention Quicken writes and it is worth confirming
Details against the file being migrated, because a wrong reading here changes
Details a share count by a factor of ten.
Examples: SplitRatio
| QField | Ratio | HeldBefore | HeldAfter | PriceBefore | PriceAfter | Notes       |
| 20     | 2     | 100        | 200       | 100.0000    | 50.0000    | Two for one |
| 30     | 3     | 100        | 300       | 120.0000    | 40.0000    | Three for one |
| 15     | 1.5   | 100        | 150       | 90.0000     | 60.0000    | Three for two |
| 5      | 0.5   | 100        | 50        | 50.0000     | 100.0000   | A reverse split |

Attributes SplitRatio
| Attribute   | Type    | Default |
| QField      | Decimal | 0       |
| Ratio       | Decimal | 0       |
| HeldBefore  | Shares  | 0       |
| HeldAfter   | Shares  | 0       |
| PriceBefore | Price   | 0       |
| PriceAfter  | Price   | 0       |
| Notes       | String  | none    |

