# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Invoices, and when their income is recognised
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

Description Income from an invoice is recognised when the invoice is paid, not
Description when it is issued. The reports being compared against are on a cash
Description basis, and that is what cash basis means.
Details
Details This section says what the QIF export makes possible, which is less than
Details the rule asks for, and it says so rather than approximating quietly.

$WIP
BusinessRule How the invoice section is shaped
Description Two kinds of record share the section, told apart by the L field.
Details Observed in the business file: 425 records, 212 invoices and 213
Details payments. The counts are almost equal because almost every invoice was
Details paid.
Examples: InvoiceRecordKind
| Kind    | LField           | HasSplitLines | CarriesCategories | Count |
| Invoice | --Split--        | true          | true              | 207   |
| Invoice | An income category | false       | true              | 5     |
| Payment | A bracketed account | false      | false             | 213   |

Attributes InvoiceRecordKind
| Attribute         | Type    | Default |
| Kind              | String  |         |
| LField            | String  |         |
| HasSplitLines     | Boolean | false   |
| CarriesCategories | Boolean | false   |
| Count             | String  |         |

$WIP
BusinessRule What the N field is, and why nothing is posted from it
Description N on an invoice is the invoice number and N on a payment is the
Description number of the invoice being paid, which an earlier reading of this
Description file missed: it examined XI, a record-type flag with two values
Description across all 425 records, and did not look at N.
Details The link is real. 194 of the 212 invoices carry N and 176 of the 213
Details payments do; in 156 cases the N matches, the amount agrees and the
Details payee agrees as well, all 156 of them, which is not a coincidence that
Details is available. Payments also carry the number with a letter appended,
Details one per instalment: 2820a, 2820b, 2820c and 2820d come to invoice 2820
Details exactly, and two payments of 4,000.00 settle invoice 2050 of 8,000.00.
Details
Details It is not complete enough to post from, which is what matters here. Not
Details one of the 32 inter-company invoices has a payment carrying its number.
Details 37 payments carry no N at all. Numbers are reused, and some payments
Details carry what looks like the customer's own cheque number instead.
Details
Details Reconstructing the allocation was tried twelve ways -- by N, by N with
Details the instalment suffix stripped, by payee and amount, by letting a
Details combined payment run on to the next open invoice, with and without
Details credit notes offset -- and the best of them still put uncollected
Details Consulting at -80.65 against the 975.00 that is wanted. So the N field
Details is recorded here as a fact about the format and is not used to decide a
Details figure. The cleared marker below is used instead, and it is one field.
Examples: InvoiceLinkEvidence
| Question                                      | Answer                                       |
| Do payments carry categories                  | No; 0 of 213 have split lines                |
| Is there a reference field                    | Yes; N, on 176 of 213 payments               |
| Does it identify the invoice                  | Often; 156 agree on N, amount and payee      |
| Does it survive an instalment                 | Yes; 2820a to 2820d come to invoice 2820     |
| Is it on every payment                        | No; 37 carry none, and no inter-company one  |
| Is it enough to post income from              | No; twelve reconstructions all missed        |
| What was XI                                   | A record-type flag; 1 is a document, 3 a payment |

Attributes InvoiceLinkEvidence
| Attribute | Type   | Default |
| Question  | String |         |
| Answer    | String |         |

BusinessRule The cleared marker says whether an invoice was collected
Description Quicken marks a document cleared once the money is in, and leaves
Description the C field off one that is still outstanding. That is the whole
Description test, and it is exact.
Details 203 of the 212 documents in the business file carry C*, and the nine
Details that carry nothing hold 975.00 of Consulting, 378.75 of Uncategorized
Details Income - Business and no Royalty. Those are each of the three figures
Details the all-dates report gives, to the cent.
Details
Details Eight of the nine have no payment carrying their number either, which
Details agrees. The ninth, Convregence for 300.00, does have one -- so it was
Details paid and never marked -- and Quicken's own report leaves its 300.00 out
Details as well. The marker is followed rather than second-guessed, because
Details following it reproduces the report including that inconsistency.
Details
Details It governs income and not expense, which was measured rather than
Details assumed. Four of the nine are reimbursement invoices to Ken's own
Details companies and their lines are expense categories, not income: they are
Details claims to be paid back for money already spent on a personal card.
Details Quicken credits those whether or not the invoice has been collected.
Details Treating all nine alike moved 2025 expenses from -198,939.00, which
Details agrees with Quicken to the cent, to -212,342.46 -- out by 13,403.46,
Details exactly the two reimbursement invoices outstanding at the export.
Examples: CollectedTest
| CField | Bills      | Documents | Recognised                              |
| *      | Income     | 203       | Yes; its categories are income          |
| (none) | Income     | 5         | No; none of it is income                |
| (none) | An expense | 4         | Yes; the expense is credited regardless |

Attributes CollectedTest
| Attribute  | Type    | Default |
| CField     | String  |         |
| Bills      | String  |         |
| Documents  | Integer | 0       |
| Recognised | String  |         |

$WIP
BusinessRule What the cash basis is worth, measured against the all-dates report
Description Quicken's all-dates report is itself on a cash basis, so the gap
Description between it and an accrual reading is exactly what was invoiced and
Description never collected. That gave three equations, and the cleared marker
Description satisfies all three.
Details Ken confirmed the first of them from his own records before the code was
Details written: an unpaid invoice from 2008 for 975.00. A report difference
Details predicted a fact about the business and the fact held.
Examples: CashBasisTarget
| Category                        | QuickenAllDates | OnAccrual | Uncollected | Ours      |
| Consulting                      | 311128.75       | 312103.75 | 975.00      | 311128.75 |
| Royalty                         | 20977.40        | 20977.40  | 0.00        | 20977.40  |
| Uncategorized Income - Business | 43770.73        | 44149.48  | 378.75      | 43770.73  |

Attributes CashBasisTarget
| Attribute       | Type  | Default |
| Category        | Text  | none    |
| QuickenAllDates | Money | 0.00    |
| OnAccrual       | Money | 0.00    |
| Uncollected     | Money | 0.00    |
| Ours            | Money | 0.00    |

BusinessRule Where an invoice that was never collected is parked
Description It cannot credit an income category, because no money came. It
Description cannot credit nothing, because then the book would not balance and a
Description trial balance would be out by the amount outstanding. So it credits
Description a holding account, and the receivable stands against it.
Details It is a real account, which is what keeps it out of a spending report,
Details and its balance is the whole of the income that was invoiced and never
Details earned: 907.80 in the business file, being 975.00 of Consulting and
Details 378.75 of Uncategorized Income - Business less a credit note of 445.95.
Details That is the figure that answers "is anything outstanding", because the
Details receivable itself nets to zero -- payments in that file come to the same
Details total as invoices even though five invoices are open, which is an
Details inconsistency in the source and not in the import.
Details
Details A collected invoice is posted in its own period, as it always was, and
Details its receivable and categories are the two sides of one transaction. So
Details is an uncollected one that bills for an expense rather than income.
Details
Details The asset holding account is the symmetric case, for a bill whose lines
Details are income. Neither file in testdata has one, so it is specified and
Details untested.
Examples: InvoiceHoldingAccount
| Document | DocumentAccount            | HoldingAccount                  |
| Invoice  | Assets:Customer~Invoices   | Liabilities:Unrecognised~Income |
| Bill     | Liabilities:Business~Bills | Assets:Unrecognised~Expense     |

Attributes InvoiceHoldingAccount
| Attribute       | Type        | Default |
| Document        | String      |         |
| DocumentAccount | AccountPath |         |
| HoldingAccount  | AccountPath |         |

BusinessRule Which period a collected invoice is reported in
Description Its own, not the date the money arrived. This is a deviation from a
Description strict cash basis and it is deliberate, because the alternative
Description cannot be done honestly from this export.
Details The payment date is not recoverable for a large part of the file: no
Details inter-company invoice has a payment carrying its number and 37 payments
Details carry none at all, so dating recognition by payment means guessing the
Details date for those. Measured, guessing it moved 2021 expenses from 7,500.00
Details away from Quicken to 27,777.72 away, and 2022 from 7,500.00 to
Details 25,196.24. Posting in the invoice's own period left every one of those
Details figures where it already was.
Details
Details The all-dates totals are the same under either reading, because an
Details invoice collected at all is collected once. Only the year moves, and
Details only for an invoice that crossed a year end before being paid.
Details
Details Put to Ken with the measurement above, and accepted: the deviation is
Details fine. So this is a settled choice and not a thing to revisit when the
Details next QIF arrives.
Examples: RecognitionPeriod
| Case                                    | ReportedIn           | Why                               |
| Invoiced and collected in the same year | That year            | The two readings agree            |
| Invoiced one year, collected the next   | The year invoiced    | The payment date is not reliable  |
| Invoiced and never collected            | Not reported at all  | No money came                     |

Attributes RecognitionPeriod
| Attribute   | Type   | Default |
| Case        | String |         |
| ReportedIn  | String |         |
| Why         | String |         |

Scenario A collected invoice is income in its own period
Description Marked cleared, so the money came. The receivable and the category
Description are the two sides of one transaction, exactly as a bank record with
Description a category is.
