Scenario An invoice section posts to the receivables account
Description An invoice is money owed to the business, which is an asset, and a
Description bill is money owed by it. Neither needs anything beyond the two
Description postings every other transaction has. When the income is recognised
Description is a separate question; see the invoice section further down.
Given the file contains
"""
!Option:AutoSwitch
!Account
NInvoices
TInvoice
^
NBills
TBill
^
"""
When qif file imported
Then accounts created are : ChartOfAccounts
| Path              | Type               | Placeholder |
| Assets            | AccountsReceivable | true        |
| Assets:Invoices   | AccountsReceivable | false       |
| Liabilities       | AccountsPayable    | true        |
| Liabilities:Bills | AccountsPayable    | false       |
# A receivable and a payable have types of their own now that the Business
# group exists, where before they were filed as a plain asset and a plain debt.
# The root takes the type of the first account created under it, which is why
# Assets reads as a receivable here -- a wrinkle of the importer, not of the
# types, and the roots are renamed afterwards anyway.

$WIP
