# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What needs checking against the file being migrated
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

$WIP
BusinessRule What the two files settled, and what is still assumed
Description Each point was a place where being wrong would be expensive and
Description quiet. Most are now settled by reading the files in testdata. The
Description ones still marked Assumed have no evidence either way in those
Description files, and would only matter to a different export.
Examples: DialectRisk
| Point                  | Status  | Evidence                                                                 |
| Date order             | Settled | 24,324 dates have a second part above 12 and none a first part above 12  |
| Century marker         | Settled | Apostrophe year tokens run " 5" to "26" with no gap: two thousands       |
| Blank-padded year      | Settled | "6/17' 5" is June 2005; the year is padded as well as the day            |
| Stock split ratio      | Settled | The one split was a four-for-one and Q is 40, so Q is the ratio times ten |
| Split line signs       | Settled | All 1,045 split records sum exactly to T; 268 have lines of both signs   |
| Split category source  | Settled | 1,026 records carry the literal --Split-- in L; the split lines hold the categories |
| Category list presence | Settled | Present in both; every declared category carries E or I, none neither    |
| Undeclared categories  | Settled | One name in the personal file and five in the business one; the sign decides |
| Amount fields          | Settled | U equals T in all 42,322 transaction records; they differ only in a template |
| Cleared markers        | Settled | All four occur: X, star, c, and R once                                   |
| File encoding          | Settled | One file is UTF-8 and the other Windows-1252; decided by trying          |
| Statement balance      | Settled | No account block carries one, so the import cannot check itself          |
| Price list             | Settled | Absent from both, so a holding is priced from its last transaction       |
| Security symbols       | Settled | None of the 44 securities has one; the name is the identifier            |
| Transfer halves        | Settled | Both written, but only 3,053 of 4,025 pairs share a date; 558 are one day apart and 19 more than ten |
| Multi-line values      | Assumed | A field that will not parse continues the one before                     |
| Decimal comma          | Assumed | Not present in either file; kept for a European export                   |

