$WIP
Scenario Transfer pairing is the one unsettled rule that matters at scale
Description There are 8,228 bracketed category fields in the business file, so
Description a wrong pairing rule is wrong thousands of times. The counts are
Description therefore in the migration report, where they can be checked
Description against what Quicken says the balances are. See
Description AcceptanceAgainstQuicken.
Given the chart of accounts is : ChartOfAccounts
| Path                   | Type    | Placeholder |
| Expenses:Uncategorized | Expense | false       |
Given the file contains
"""
!Option:AutoSwitch
!Account
NChecking
TBank
^
NSavings
TBank
^
!Clear:AutoSwitch
!Account
NChecking
TBank
^
!Type:Bank
D3/ 1'24
T-500.00
PTransfer
L[Savings]
^
!Account
NSavings
TBank
^
!Type:Bank
D3/ 1'24
T500.00
PTransfer
L[Checking]
^
"""
When qif file imported
Then transfer pairing report is : TransferPairingReport Vertical
| BracketedFields | 2 |
| PairsFormed     | 1 |
| Unpaired        | 0 |
| NearMisses      | 0 |

